atson Park Creek, Dry\nGulch, Happy Canyon Creek, Lake Gulch, South Platte River and\nEast Toll Gate Creek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1\ninch are expected over the area. This additional rain will result\nin minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSouthern Aurora, eastern Centennial, Castle Rock, Parker, Lone\nTree, Larkspur, Castle Pines, Franktown, Sedalia, The Pinery,\nPerry Park, Ponderosa Park, Devil's Head, Arapahoe Park,\nFoxfield, Castlewood Canyon and Shamballa.","ends":"2026-07-29T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.13e662d6e196dc40e2d5e38b16af1442896771da.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.13e662d6e196dc40e2d5e38b16af1442896771da.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-07-29T17:51:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 291751 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1151 AM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers and thunderstorms likely across the high terrain in the late morning, shifting to the plains by the afternoon. - Strong storms could produce localized flash flooding, particularly for the burn scar and areas along and east of the southern I-25 Cor","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-07-29T09:17:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today and tonight... Monsoon moisture will bring another round of widespread showers and thunderstorms for the high terrain and plains this afternoon and evening. Localized heavy rainfall is possible, particularly for the burn scars and areas along and east of the I-25 Corridor. Overnight humidity recoveries will be excellent across the region. LONG TERM DISCUSSION...Thursday through","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"cht01","stati